1
00:00:00,268 --> 00:00:02,137
I'm going to say this for the first time.

2
00:00:02,137 --> 00:00:05,707
My real name is Joycelyn Trinidad.

3
00:00:05,707 --> 00:00:07,133
I'll let you know

4
00:00:07,133 --> 00:00:10,846
once the magazine publishes
your shoot and interview, Savana.

5
00:00:10,846 --> 00:00:12,314
I mean, Joyce.

6
00:00:12,314 --> 00:00:14,800
Via, thank you so much.

7
00:00:14,801 --> 00:00:16,399
Do we have a problem, Via?

8
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:17,300
You tell me.

9
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,506
Is there something I need to worry about?

10
00:00:19,506 --> 00:00:21,108
What did you do?

11
00:00:21,108 --> 00:00:23,610
Who did you tell your real name to?

12
00:00:23,610 --> 00:00:26,213
I only told one person, Mommy.

13
00:00:26,213 --> 00:00:30,649
It's so convenient
that right after I tell you my real name,

14
00:00:30,649 --> 00:00:32,920
Girl with Periwinkle Hair released her video

15
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:34,254
and even dragged my father into it.

16
00:00:34,254 --> 00:00:36,323
My whole life is now out in the open.

17
00:00:36,323 --> 00:00:38,058
I admired what you did.

18
00:00:38,058 --> 00:00:39,526
I have no control over the minds of people

19
00:00:39,526 --> 00:00:42,329
who give malice to what you confessed, okay?

20
00:00:42,329 --> 00:00:45,565
I'm sorry, Via.
I just can't bear all the bashing.

21
00:00:45,565 --> 00:00:46,685
Get out of my office.

22
00:00:46,685 --> 00:00:50,003
Because of the recent issue about Savana,

23
00:00:50,003 --> 00:00:52,039
we decided to remove her from Josh's movie.

24
00:00:52,039 --> 00:00:55,142
Remove me from the project, but retain Joyce.

25
00:00:55,142 --> 00:00:59,645
Joyce will stay in the film
if you return to Casa Fuerte.

26
00:01:22,669 --> 00:01:24,004
Mom?

27
00:01:24,004 --> 00:01:26,252
Don't tell me
you're going to confess something.

28
00:01:26,252 --> 00:01:27,966
Huh?

29
00:01:27,966 --> 00:01:30,567
What are we doing in an orphanage?

30
00:01:30,567 --> 00:01:32,145
[Bahay Aruga]
Am I adopted?

31
00:01:32,145 --> 00:01:33,413
Silly!

32
00:01:33,413 --> 00:01:36,149
I was the one who gave birth to you.

33
00:01:36,149 --> 00:01:38,518
What are we doing here, then?

34
00:01:38,518 --> 00:01:41,521
You said you have a problem, right?

35
00:01:41,521 --> 00:01:45,092
You should rest once in a while.

36
00:01:45,092 --> 00:01:47,594
I come here once a week.

37
00:01:47,594 --> 00:01:50,031
I cook for the kids.

38
00:01:50,031 --> 00:01:55,837
Once you get inside
and see the smile on the kids' faces,

39
00:01:55,837 --> 00:02:00,108
you'll forget all about your problems.

40
00:02:00,108 --> 00:02:07,047
You might realize somehow,
that you need to apologize to Via.

41
00:02:08,549 --> 00:02:10,385
- Oh...
- Good morning.

42
00:02:10,385 --> 00:02:11,753
Hello, Sister.

43
00:02:11,753 --> 00:02:13,621
This is my son, Liam.

44
00:02:13,621 --> 00:02:15,690
Hi, Liam. Good morning.

45
00:02:15,690 --> 00:02:16,891
Good morning, too.

46
00:02:16,891 --> 00:02:19,460
Good morning, my dearies!

47
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:25,033
We're now here in Bahay Aruga orphanage!

48
00:02:25,033 --> 00:02:28,368
I said this is for good publicity.

49
00:02:30,939 --> 00:02:33,741
So here it is, my dearies!

50
00:02:33,741 --> 00:02:37,745
We're here with the one and only, Savana.

51
00:02:37,745 --> 00:02:41,215
Savana, please say hi to our viewers.

52
00:02:41,215 --> 00:02:43,952
Good morning! Savana just woke up.

53
00:02:43,952 --> 00:02:45,320
Smile!

54
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:46,921
Smile, girl! There.

55
00:02:46,921 --> 00:02:51,125
Later, Savana and I will have a coffee date.

56
00:02:51,125 --> 00:02:55,185
So, I'll also interview her
about her gifts for the kids

57
00:02:55,185 --> 00:02:58,132
in Bahay Aruga.

58
00:02:58,132 --> 00:02:59,968
Almost every week, we're here in...

59
00:02:59,968 --> 00:03:01,736
Actually, the angle there is nicer.

60
00:03:01,736 --> 00:03:03,604
- Let's go there.
- Okay. Let's see.

61
00:03:03,604 --> 00:03:06,641
- Take your camera over there.
- Wait.

62
00:03:06,641 --> 00:03:08,476
Savana.

63
00:03:08,476 --> 00:03:11,445
I mean, Joyce.

64
00:03:13,448 --> 00:03:14,982
Liam?

65
00:03:18,328 --> 00:03:20,655
My dear, who's that?

66
00:03:20,655 --> 00:03:22,423
He's good-looking.

67
00:03:22,423 --> 00:03:25,194
He's the creative manager of her movie.

68
00:03:25,194 --> 00:03:26,661
Creative manager?

69
00:03:26,661 --> 00:03:28,429
Is he single?

70
00:03:28,429 --> 00:03:30,665
Let's go over there. Let's work. Come on.

71
00:03:30,665 --> 00:03:32,132
Let's go.

72
00:03:35,436 --> 00:03:36,804
Come on.

73
00:03:37,472 --> 00:03:38,506
Good morning.

74
00:03:38,506 --> 00:03:41,309
Good morning, good morning.

75
00:03:41,309 --> 00:03:47,012
We're so happy to be here.
So excited, my goodness.

76
00:03:47,012 --> 00:03:50,849
Do you want to come back some other day, son?

77
00:03:53,855 --> 00:03:55,056
No need.

78
00:03:55,056 --> 00:03:57,157
We're here anyway.

79
00:04:03,698 --> 00:04:05,867
- Thank you.
- Okay.

80
00:04:05,867 --> 00:04:07,235
Here.

81
00:04:07,235 --> 00:04:08,503
- Here. Juice.
- Here.

82
00:04:08,503 --> 00:04:11,839
- Juice.
- Get a fork over there.

83
00:04:11,839 --> 00:04:13,708
Hi!

84
00:04:13,708 --> 00:04:16,711
You can use this for your lesson, right?

85
00:04:16,711 --> 00:04:19,947
I don't use a coloring book anymore.

86
00:04:20,982 --> 00:04:22,183
Just take it.

87
00:04:22,183 --> 00:04:23,317
Thank you.

88
00:04:23,317 --> 00:04:24,652
Mommy...

89
00:04:24,652 --> 00:04:26,387
Come on, smile.

90
00:04:26,387 --> 00:04:28,489
Smile.

91
00:04:28,489 --> 00:04:31,058
Hi! Here. Give it to her.

92
00:04:32,393 --> 00:04:34,062
You're so beautiful.

93
00:04:34,062 --> 00:04:38,533
The nuns and I have been
watching you in Captive Hearts.

94
00:04:38,533 --> 00:04:41,301
Thank you. You're so pretty too.

95
00:04:43,571 --> 00:04:44,672
- Hi, my dearies.
- Mommy...

96
00:04:44,672 --> 00:04:46,074
Hurry up, come here. Come and get it.

97
00:04:46,074 --> 00:04:48,242
- Here, here, here.
- There you go.

98
00:04:48,242 --> 00:04:51,079
Baby, say hi. Say hi to my vlog.

99
00:04:51,079 --> 00:04:52,947
Hi, my dearies!

100
00:04:52,947 --> 00:04:55,883
Hi!

101
00:04:55,883 --> 00:04:58,750
Mommy, let's stop.

102
00:04:58,750 --> 00:05:01,137
I'm going to do this sincerely,
but not like this.

103
00:05:01,137 --> 00:05:03,758
We're using the kids.

104
00:05:03,758 --> 00:05:06,994
Come on, just smile. Smile!

105
00:05:13,101 --> 00:05:14,936
Give it to her.

106
00:05:14,936 --> 00:05:15,937
- Give it to her.
- Hi!

107
00:05:15,937 --> 00:05:17,371
Hello.

108
00:05:17,371 --> 00:05:18,773
That looks so nice.

109
00:05:18,773 --> 00:05:20,241
Wait, I want to join you.

110
00:05:20,241 --> 00:05:22,710
There, it's so beautiful.

111
00:05:22,710 --> 00:05:23,778
Picture!

112
00:05:23,778 --> 00:05:27,679
Picture? Okay, game, game, game.
One, two, three.

113
00:05:27,679 --> 00:05:31,557
Hi! There you go. One more. The next one.

114
00:05:34,822 --> 00:05:39,259
Baby, say hi to the camera.

115
00:05:41,262 --> 00:05:43,231
I'll just refill this one.

116
00:05:43,231 --> 00:05:44,932
Okay.

117
00:05:51,739 --> 00:05:53,240
Joyce?

118
00:05:54,675 --> 00:05:56,944
Can you help me here?

119
00:05:58,533 --> 00:06:00,314
Okay.

120
00:06:00,314 --> 00:06:01,782
Wait!

121
00:06:06,087 --> 00:06:07,088
Here.

122
00:06:07,088 --> 00:06:10,361
For you. Look at the camera.

123
00:06:13,794 --> 00:06:15,363
Okay, next.

124
00:06:15,363 --> 00:06:17,798
- Next.
- Next.

125
00:06:17,798 --> 00:06:21,169
My dear Aunt, what do we serve the kids?

126
00:06:21,169 --> 00:06:22,770
Don't focus the camera on me.

127
00:06:22,770 --> 00:06:25,640
I'm not a celebrity who needs attention.

128
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:27,341
Okay. I'll just focus on the food.

129
00:06:27,341 --> 00:06:28,642
Yes.

130
00:06:39,887 --> 00:06:42,089
Go ahead. Laugh.

131
00:06:44,692 --> 00:06:45,993
What?

132
00:06:47,662 --> 00:06:49,596
Laugh.

133
00:06:51,363 --> 00:06:55,970
I know what I do for publicity
is so pathetic.

134
00:07:02,376 --> 00:07:04,678
You know, ever since...

135
00:07:05,379 --> 00:07:07,647
I started working with you...

136
00:07:08,416 --> 00:07:11,752
I've learned a lot of things about showbiz.

137
00:07:11,752 --> 00:07:14,154
So I won't be surprised by this.

138
00:07:20,861 --> 00:07:23,230
I'm sorry if...

139
00:07:24,112 --> 00:07:26,246
if I called you.

140
00:07:27,235 --> 00:07:30,037
I just wanted to check on you.

141
00:07:31,505 --> 00:07:36,376
Even though I knew you wanted to be alone.

142
00:07:38,546 --> 00:07:41,148
My mom took my phone.

143
00:07:45,253 --> 00:07:48,522
I'm still sorry for all the things
you're going through.

144
00:07:51,759 --> 00:07:54,027
I'm used to it.

145
00:07:55,730 --> 00:07:57,932
Tomorrow.

146
00:07:57,932 --> 00:07:59,600
Tomorrow...

147
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:04,438
I'm sure there will be a new rumor
that people will obsess about.

148
00:08:07,942 --> 00:08:11,344
You probably heard about what I did to Via.

149
00:08:16,550 --> 00:08:18,786
Liam, I want to...

150
00:08:18,786 --> 00:08:23,123
I want to apologize to her,
but she won't answer my calls.

151
00:08:25,357 --> 00:08:30,094
I want to be given a chance
to apologize to her in person.

152
00:08:32,166 --> 00:08:33,968
Don't worry.

153
00:08:33,968 --> 00:08:35,869
I'll talk to her.

154
00:08:38,639 --> 00:08:40,373
Thank you.

155
00:08:47,114 --> 00:08:51,952
Joyce, I also have something to confess...

156
00:08:58,359 --> 00:09:01,561
about our movie.

157
00:09:02,997 --> 00:09:07,935
The movie will push through...

158
00:09:07,935 --> 00:09:12,506
because I made a deal with
my dad and Uncle Ramon.

159
00:09:17,290 --> 00:09:19,091
What deal?

160
00:09:27,955 --> 00:09:29,357
I don't have it.

161
00:09:29,357 --> 00:09:31,359
You do! You took it!

162
00:09:31,359 --> 00:09:34,395
- I said I don't have it.
- You do!

163
00:09:34,395 --> 00:09:37,296
- I said I don't have it.
- You do!

164
00:09:37,296 --> 00:09:38,564
I don't have it.

165
00:09:38,564 --> 00:09:40,566
You do! You took it!

166
00:09:40,566 --> 00:09:42,701
- I said I don't have it.
- You do!

167
00:09:42,701 --> 00:09:43,969
You took it from me!

168
00:09:43,969 --> 00:09:45,304
- Give it back!
- I don't have it!

169
00:09:45,304 --> 00:09:46,505
- Dex!
- You do!

170
00:09:46,505 --> 00:09:49,006
- I don't have it!
- You do!

171
00:09:51,176 --> 00:09:53,678
- I don't have it!
- You do!

172
00:09:57,215 --> 00:09:58,417
Dex!

173
00:09:58,417 --> 00:10:00,285
Dex! Kid.

174
00:10:00,285 --> 00:10:01,820
Where's the kid you were chasing earlier?

175
00:10:01,820 --> 00:10:04,889
He'll be dead meat once Bating catches him.

176
00:10:11,430 --> 00:10:12,897
Liam?

177
00:10:14,951 --> 00:10:16,819
Who are you looking for?

178
00:10:20,772 --> 00:10:24,008
Don't worry about it.
I just thought I saw something.

179
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:37,441
Dex?

180
00:10:45,464 --> 00:10:46,710
Dex.

181
00:11:08,721 --> 00:11:10,790
<i>You're dead meat, Daddy.</i>

182
00:11:10,790 --> 00:11:13,092
Mom is mad at you again.

183
00:11:13,092 --> 00:11:17,163
That's how much your mom loves.

184
00:11:17,163 --> 00:11:18,864
So, let's go?

185
00:11:23,052 --> 00:11:24,593
My boy...

186
00:12:02,842 --> 00:12:05,144
Who is Dex?

187
00:12:05,144 --> 00:12:07,179
My name's Sep.

188
00:12:20,960 --> 00:12:22,629
Sep, come here.

189
00:12:22,629 --> 00:12:24,364
Give me my pencil back.

190
00:12:24,364 --> 00:12:25,832
I said I don't have it.

191
00:12:25,832 --> 00:12:27,033
Give it to me!

192
00:12:27,033 --> 00:12:29,235
You have it. Give me my pencil back.

193
00:12:29,235 --> 00:12:31,571
I said no. I don't have it.

194
00:12:31,571 --> 00:12:32,905
Oops!

195
00:12:32,905 --> 00:12:37,310
Hey, that's enough.
Fighting is not a good thing.

196
00:12:37,310 --> 00:12:40,546
I will tell on you.

197
00:12:40,546 --> 00:12:42,281
Let's go.

198
00:12:56,496 --> 00:12:58,631
Are you okay?

199
00:12:58,631 --> 00:13:02,268
Yes. I'm used to Bating.

200
00:13:02,268 --> 00:13:04,737
They always pick on me.

201
00:13:04,737 --> 00:13:06,138
Is that so?

202
00:13:07,006 --> 00:13:09,641
Always be a good kid.

203
00:13:13,680 --> 00:13:15,481
Hi, Sep.

204
00:13:17,083 --> 00:13:18,033
Can I see

205
00:13:18,033 --> 00:13:21,386
if you've tried anything
in your coloring book?

206
00:13:22,021 --> 00:13:24,156
Come on, let's color.

207
00:13:26,793 --> 00:13:28,460
Let me see.

208
00:13:29,307 --> 00:13:31,931
Joyce... Dex.

209
00:13:31,931 --> 00:13:33,418
My wife and son.

210
00:13:33,418 --> 00:13:36,703
You've got a lot of rubber bands on your arm.

211
00:13:36,703 --> 00:13:39,372
Do you like it?

212
00:13:39,372 --> 00:13:40,100
Yes.

213
00:13:40,100 --> 00:13:44,911
I used to like rubber bands too
when I was a kid.

214
00:13:44,911 --> 00:13:47,981
And I used to like doing stars.

215
00:13:47,981 --> 00:13:50,117
Do you know how to do it?

216
00:13:50,117 --> 00:13:51,151
No.

217
00:13:51,151 --> 00:13:53,120
Do you want me to teach you?

218
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:55,123
Let me have a rubber band.

219
00:13:55,123 --> 00:13:56,391
Do this.

220
00:13:56,391 --> 00:13:58,159
Put it down first.

221
00:13:58,159 --> 00:14:01,428
You should hold it like this.

222
00:14:02,830 --> 00:14:12,253
Insert it like this, then reach it here,
then turn it like this.

223
00:14:15,316 --> 00:14:17,345
One more.

224
00:14:17,345 --> 00:14:21,315
Reach for it, then turn it like this.

225
00:14:26,154 --> 00:14:37,373
Place it here on your thumb.
Pull it out. Like that.

226
00:14:40,668 --> 00:14:42,604
Can I see?

227
00:14:42,604 --> 00:14:44,371
Let me see.

228
00:14:52,347 --> 00:14:55,283
Liam, we've given all the kids their food.

229
00:14:55,283 --> 00:14:57,017
Thank you, Mom.

230
00:14:59,754 --> 00:15:00,755
Hello.

231
00:15:00,755 --> 00:15:02,690
Have you eaten yet?

232
00:15:02,690 --> 00:15:04,222
Not yet.

233
00:15:04,222 --> 00:15:05,341
Not yet?

234
00:15:05,341 --> 00:15:09,794
Here. Luckily, there's still one left.

235
00:15:09,794 --> 00:15:11,857
Spaghetti.

236
00:15:12,466 --> 00:15:13,635
Thank you.

237
00:15:13,635 --> 00:15:16,104
Oh, dear.

238
00:15:16,104 --> 00:15:18,573
You're so sweet.

239
00:15:18,573 --> 00:15:22,376
You were like Liam when he was a kid.

240
00:15:23,244 --> 00:15:25,679
You're so handsome.

241
00:15:28,149 --> 00:15:30,217
Go eat.

242
00:15:32,285 --> 00:15:35,687
Savana, let's go. We're done here.

243
00:15:37,158 --> 00:15:40,595
Are you leaving too, Liam?

244
00:15:40,595 --> 00:15:42,296
Auntie Tess?

245
00:15:45,833 --> 00:15:49,136
Maybe we'll stay a little longer.

246
00:15:49,930 --> 00:15:51,898
Why, son?

247
00:15:53,007 --> 00:15:55,142
Savana, come on.

248
00:16:04,483 --> 00:16:06,686
Bye.

249
00:16:06,686 --> 00:16:08,254
Thank you.

250
00:16:08,254 --> 00:16:11,990
I really didn't get Bating's pencil.

251
00:16:13,192 --> 00:16:18,030
Don't indulge someone who is
picking a fight with you, okay?

252
00:16:18,030 --> 00:16:20,266
Tell the nuns instead.

253
00:16:20,266 --> 00:16:21,959
Yes, Miss Savana.

254
00:16:21,959 --> 00:16:24,203
Promise.

255
00:16:24,203 --> 00:16:26,772
Just call me Joyce.

256
00:16:26,772 --> 00:16:29,808
Yes, Miss Joyce.

257
00:16:32,144 --> 00:16:35,013
Liam, see you at Blacksmith.

258
00:16:45,825 --> 00:16:49,027
Son, why are we staying?

259
00:16:52,932 --> 00:16:54,767
Sep?

260
00:16:54,767 --> 00:16:58,237
Where is the nun's office?

261
00:16:58,237 --> 00:16:59,871
Over there.

262
00:17:20,467 --> 00:17:24,397
[Bahay Aruga]

263
00:17:24,397 --> 00:17:26,432
Can you draw a tree?

264
00:17:26,432 --> 00:17:29,551
- Let me see.
- Later.

265
00:17:30,169 --> 00:17:31,833
I will make a...

266
00:17:31,834 --> 00:17:34,333
What are you drawing?

267
00:17:34,334 --> 00:17:36,075
Is that me?

268
00:17:36,075 --> 00:17:37,744
He is Sep.

269
00:17:37,745 --> 00:17:41,627
Stefano Lualhati is his real name.

270
00:17:41,627 --> 00:17:45,618
He came here just recently.

271
00:17:45,618 --> 00:17:47,753
They said he is from Verde Village.

272
00:17:49,956 --> 00:17:53,892
Based on our records, he's already orphaned.

273
00:17:58,130 --> 00:17:59,965
Verde Village?

274
00:18:07,206 --> 00:18:08,841
Why, Liam?

275
00:18:08,841 --> 00:18:11,643
Do you know the kid's parents?

276
00:18:12,478 --> 00:18:15,780
You're the reason we're suffering.

277
00:18:15,780 --> 00:18:16,667
They're humans.

278
00:18:16,667 --> 00:18:20,999
They are not flies you can shoo away
from their homes.

279
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:25,071
Even though you took the wrong path,

280
00:18:25,071 --> 00:18:30,804
the heart will lead you to the right way.

281
00:18:32,298 --> 00:18:34,374
No, Sister.

282
00:18:38,504 --> 00:18:42,908
Sorry. I was shocked.

283
00:18:42,908 --> 00:18:51,401
I thought he is here
because he got separated from his parents.

284
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:55,041
Turns out he's an orphan.

285
00:18:58,823 --> 00:19:00,425
I'll go ahead.

286
00:19:00,425 --> 00:19:02,927
Thank you so much, Sister.

287
00:19:12,905 --> 00:19:14,940
No, it's my brother.

288
00:19:14,940 --> 00:19:16,442
It's made out of his name.

289
00:19:17,910 --> 00:19:20,045
Royce. R...

290
00:19:20,979 --> 00:19:22,448
How was it, son?

291
00:19:22,448 --> 00:19:24,716
Did you get what you needed?

292
00:19:25,584 --> 00:19:27,046
Yes.

293
00:19:27,046 --> 00:19:31,990
I was told that Sep was from Verde Village.

294
00:19:31,990 --> 00:19:35,961
I want to talk to Mister Nestor.
He might know Sep.

295
00:19:35,961 --> 00:19:38,696
The old man who almost killed...

296
00:19:40,299 --> 00:19:43,868
Son, why would you go back there?

297
00:19:44,856 --> 00:19:50,109
And why are you suddenly interested in Sep?

298
00:19:52,311 --> 00:19:56,533
If he's from Verde Village
and already an orphan,

299
00:19:56,534 --> 00:19:58,333
I want to know

300
00:19:58,334 --> 00:20:02,320
if Casa Fuerte has to do
with the death of his parents.

301
00:20:06,539 --> 00:20:07,940
Okay.

302
00:20:07,941 --> 00:20:10,510
I'll come with you.

303
00:20:14,019 --> 00:20:15,214
Hey.

304
00:20:15,215 --> 00:20:17,216
You have a wound.

305
00:20:18,512 --> 00:20:19,721
It's nothing.

306
00:20:19,722 --> 00:20:22,867
I can even do TikTok.

307
00:20:22,868 --> 00:20:24,835
Wow, TikTok.

308
00:20:24,836 --> 00:20:26,284
Wow!

309
00:20:28,646 --> 00:20:29,974
Gosh...

310
00:20:29,974 --> 00:20:35,399
I better bring you to the clinic
before you do TikTok.

311
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:39,291
Thank you, Sir Liam. You're so kind.

312
00:20:39,291 --> 00:20:41,627
How did you know my name?

313
00:20:41,627 --> 00:20:43,996
I heard it from Miss Joyce.

314
00:20:43,996 --> 00:20:46,665
She called you Liam.

315
00:20:46,665 --> 00:20:50,669
You're like Miss Joyce.
You're both very kind.

316
00:20:50,669 --> 00:20:54,055
I will wait for you to come back.

317
00:20:55,007 --> 00:20:58,477
Promise, I'll come back.

318
00:20:58,477 --> 00:21:00,879
But before that, I'll bring you to the clinic.

319
00:21:00,879 --> 00:21:03,862
Come on, let's go. Oh, dear.

320
00:21:12,591 --> 00:21:16,661
The orphanage was correct.

321
00:21:17,496 --> 00:21:19,865
He's now an orphan.

322
00:21:19,865 --> 00:21:21,366
What?

323
00:21:21,366 --> 00:21:23,901
Why? What happened?

324
00:21:25,404 --> 00:21:26,685
He's one reason

325
00:21:26,685 --> 00:21:31,709
why the residents of the Village are furious
at Casa Fuerte.

326
00:21:35,622 --> 00:21:39,119
His family moved to a riverside place

327
00:21:39,121 --> 00:21:45,280
when they got evicted from their home.

328
00:21:47,514 --> 00:21:56,515
His parents drowned
when the water swelled during a typhoon.

329
00:21:58,237 --> 00:22:02,908
Sep was the only one who survived.

330
00:22:02,908 --> 00:22:05,610
So even though we reconciled, Liam,

331
00:22:05,610 --> 00:22:13,658
things like this will still remind us
how your company made us suffer.

332
00:22:30,669 --> 00:22:32,504
<i>He's Sep.</i>

333
00:22:32,504 --> 00:22:35,440
<i>Stefano Lualhati is his real name.</i>

334
00:22:35,440 --> 00:22:39,444
<i>He came here just recently.</i>

335
00:22:39,444 --> 00:22:41,446
<i>They said he was from Verde Village.</i>

336
00:22:43,682 --> 00:22:47,718
<i>And based on our records,
he's already an orphan.</i>

337
00:22:54,593 --> 00:22:57,628
I thought we came here to talk.

338
00:23:03,268 --> 00:23:05,636
I'm sorry, Via.

339
00:23:07,539 --> 00:23:10,942
Thank you so much for agreeing to talk.

340
00:23:14,613 --> 00:23:17,014
I can't say no to you.

341
00:23:20,986 --> 00:23:27,658
I heard from Dad
that you backed out of Blacksmith's movie.

342
00:23:29,105 --> 00:23:33,175
I think it's a good idea
that you return to Casa Fuerte.

343
00:23:34,566 --> 00:23:41,105
In that case, I won't be forced
to get involved in the movie, either.

344
00:23:45,344 --> 00:23:48,513
I have already forgotten what Joyce did.

345
00:23:53,018 --> 00:23:56,521
Via, I also invited Joyce tonight.

346
00:24:02,060 --> 00:24:04,462
Please follow me, Sir, Ma'am.

347
00:24:05,564 --> 00:24:08,065
Mr. Herrera and his companion
are already here.

348
00:24:09,167 --> 00:24:10,669
Liam.

349
00:24:10,669 --> 00:24:12,371
Good evening.

350
00:24:12,371 --> 00:24:14,172
Via.

351
00:24:17,209 --> 00:24:20,345
- Go on.
- I can adjust the table for you.

352
00:24:20,345 --> 00:24:22,214
Yes, please. We know each other, anyway.

353
00:24:22,214 --> 00:24:24,249
That's okay.

354
00:24:24,249 --> 00:24:26,084
Come, Hans. Join us.

355
00:24:26,084 --> 00:24:27,285
Should I?

356
00:24:27,285 --> 00:24:28,487
Yeah.

357
00:24:28,487 --> 00:24:29,812
Help me.

358
00:24:32,691 --> 00:24:33,692
Let me help you.

359
00:24:33,692 --> 00:24:34,760
- It's okay. We got this.
- Everything good now?

360
00:24:34,760 --> 00:24:35,893
Okay.

361
00:24:38,463 --> 00:24:40,351
It's a bit chilly, right?

362
00:24:43,368 --> 00:24:45,704
Let's go.

363
00:24:45,704 --> 00:24:47,605
Thank you, thank you.

364
00:25:01,052 --> 00:25:02,620
Thank you.

365
00:26:17,195 --> 00:26:21,766
So, Liam, you're back from Bahay Aruga.

366
00:26:23,802 --> 00:26:25,536
How was it?

367
00:26:26,671 --> 00:26:28,439
Bahay Aruga?

368
00:26:31,877 --> 00:26:34,145
Oh, yeah.

369
00:26:35,146 --> 00:26:36,815
It's an orphanage.

370
00:26:36,815 --> 00:26:41,386
Mom brought me with her
when she visited for the kids.

371
00:26:41,386 --> 00:26:48,459
It was a coincidence
that Joyce was there, too.

372
00:26:51,329 --> 00:26:54,398
Mom and I haven't gone back there yet.

373
00:27:03,675 --> 00:27:08,980
By the way, Liam,
regarding Savana's action scenes,

374
00:27:08,980 --> 00:27:12,017
please take care of her.

375
00:27:12,017 --> 00:27:14,252
I mean, Joyce.

376
00:27:14,252 --> 00:27:17,522
Sorry. I'm not used to calling you Joyce.

377
00:27:17,522 --> 00:27:19,895
You were already using the name Savana
when I met you.

378
00:27:20,725 --> 00:27:25,564
Liam here is so used to calling her Joyce.

379
00:27:25,564 --> 00:27:28,265
It seems like
they've known each other for a long time.

380
00:27:30,735 --> 00:27:33,371
- Actually, Via...
- Via, can we talk?

381
00:27:34,239 --> 00:27:36,173
- Go ahead.
- You go first.

382
00:27:45,216 --> 00:27:47,685
They both went silent.

383
00:27:49,588 --> 00:27:52,312
Hans, just so you know,

384
00:27:52,312 --> 00:27:54,759
Liam is no longer working for Blacksmith.

385
00:27:54,759 --> 00:27:59,798
He can't keep an eye on Joyce anymore
during her action scenes.

386
00:27:59,798 --> 00:28:03,602
Sorry, he's going to return to Casa Fuerte.

387
00:28:03,602 --> 00:28:05,469
- Really?
- Yeah.

388
00:28:06,104 --> 00:28:08,773
You resigned from Blacksmith?

389
00:28:10,675 --> 00:28:13,043
What about our movie?

390
00:28:15,013 --> 00:28:17,238
Well, I guess,

391
00:28:17,238 --> 00:28:23,210
we've established
that my boyfriend has many secrets.

392
00:28:24,689 --> 00:28:25,790
Via.

393
00:28:25,790 --> 00:28:27,091
What?

394
00:28:28,193 --> 00:28:31,829
I didn't know
you and Joyce met at the orphanage.

395
00:28:32,530 --> 00:28:36,500
Joyce didn't know
that you're no longer in Blacksmith.

396
00:28:45,310 --> 00:28:47,745
Excuse me. I'll just go to the powder room.

397
00:28:53,952 --> 00:28:56,153
I'll use the restroom, too.

398
00:29:20,311 --> 00:29:21,946
Joyce.

399
00:29:26,151 --> 00:29:29,119
Is Via still mad at me?

400
00:29:32,232 --> 00:29:33,692
Hans and I can leave.

401
00:29:33,692 --> 00:29:36,627
It's okay. I'll tell him we're leaving.

402
00:29:40,498 --> 00:29:44,201
Joyce, about my resignation at Blacksmith...

403
00:29:46,538 --> 00:29:50,408
I tried to tell you
when we were at the orphanage.

404
00:29:50,408 --> 00:29:52,977
But I lost the chance.

405
00:29:57,716 --> 00:30:01,352
Did you follow me here to explain?

406
00:30:01,352 --> 00:30:06,056
Joyce, I didn't want you
to find out this way.

407
00:30:17,969 --> 00:30:20,716
Liam, I can't do anything...

408
00:30:22,862 --> 00:30:25,342
if that's your decision.

409
00:30:27,979 --> 00:30:30,447
And you don't have to explain.

410
00:31:02,581 --> 00:31:05,250
What's taking them so long?

411
00:31:06,417 --> 00:31:07,786
Maybe it's crowded.

412
00:31:07,786 --> 00:31:09,587
Probably, there's a line.

413
00:31:16,961 --> 00:31:21,599
You're the editor-in-chief
of Escale Magazine, right?

414
00:31:21,599 --> 00:31:23,133
Yeah.

415
00:31:23,868 --> 00:31:27,137
I know it's far different from Liam's job.

416
00:31:27,872 --> 00:31:31,509
You're the human rights lawyer?

417
00:31:31,509 --> 00:31:32,944
Yes.

418
00:31:32,944 --> 00:31:35,680
And far different from Joyce's job too.

419
00:31:35,680 --> 00:31:37,816
You know what they say.

420
00:31:37,816 --> 00:31:40,518
Opposites attract. Right?

421
00:31:40,518 --> 00:31:42,186
Yes, I agree.

422
00:31:43,868 --> 00:31:47,637
That's why sometimes I cannot keep up
with the things she does.

423
00:31:48,393 --> 00:31:51,496
I only watch her shows.

424
00:31:54,332 --> 00:32:00,604
It was Liam
who taught me terms regarding heavy equipment.

425
00:32:07,078 --> 00:32:09,179
To our opposites.

426
00:32:10,014 --> 00:32:11,541
To our opposites.

427
00:32:20,425 --> 00:32:24,962
So without any pretensions...

428
00:32:27,866 --> 00:32:34,371
I really wish for you
to be happy with your choice.

429
00:32:43,681 --> 00:32:46,050
I have no choice, Joyce.

430
00:32:49,854 --> 00:32:54,869
If there's something I learned
from making our movie...

431
00:32:57,528 --> 00:32:59,493
it is...

432
00:33:02,600 --> 00:33:05,269
We all have a choice.

433
00:33:09,277 --> 00:33:13,413
You taught me how to be brave.

434
00:33:15,280 --> 00:33:21,251
You taught me
to choose what I think is better for me.

435
00:33:25,757 --> 00:33:32,730
I dared to be honest with myself...

436
00:33:36,567 --> 00:33:38,969
But I went overboard.

437
00:33:41,439 --> 00:33:45,409
That's why I did Via wrong.

438
00:33:47,946 --> 00:33:50,547
I really want to talk to her.

439
00:33:55,954 --> 00:33:59,056
I don't think Via will talk to you.

440
00:34:04,332 --> 00:34:07,034
So she's still mad at me.

441
00:34:12,917 --> 00:34:14,658
Joyce-

442
00:34:16,874 --> 00:34:18,776
Don't blame yourself.

443
00:34:18,776 --> 00:34:22,446
I have no one to blame but myself.

444
00:34:24,048 --> 00:34:28,752
That is
what taking full accountability means, Liam.

445
00:34:31,990 --> 00:34:34,658
And I think that's what you should also do...

446
00:34:36,294 --> 00:34:39,797
Take full accountability
for all your decisions.

447
00:34:44,535 --> 00:34:46,336
Joyce.

448
00:34:52,577 --> 00:34:54,312
I'm sorry.

449
00:35:23,541 --> 00:35:25,410
I better check on them.

450
00:35:25,410 --> 00:35:28,246
- Are you going, too?
- Okay.

451
00:35:28,246 --> 00:35:29,847
Go ahead.

452
00:36:24,302 --> 00:36:26,703
Can I talk to you?

453
00:36:31,809 --> 00:36:34,444
I want to apologize.

454
00:36:36,096 --> 00:36:38,631
I want to apologize...

455
00:36:40,785 --> 00:36:43,587
because I know I did you wrong.

456
00:36:53,666 --> 00:36:55,800
You know what's funny?

457
00:36:57,335 --> 00:37:05,335
Before you came,
I told Liam I wasn't ready yet to see you.

458
00:37:08,813 --> 00:37:11,893
But Liam advised me...

459
00:37:13,452 --> 00:37:16,217
to put myself in your shoes...

460
00:37:18,623 --> 00:37:21,925
so I could understand why you did that.

461
00:37:25,663 --> 00:37:31,601
And because I love Liam,
I'll heed his advice.

462
00:37:32,537 --> 00:37:35,038
I'll understand.

463
00:37:38,476 --> 00:37:40,377
Thank you, Via.

464
00:37:41,245 --> 00:37:43,847
Thank you. I'm sorry.

465
00:37:45,316 --> 00:37:47,484
I'm so sorry.

466
00:37:50,888 --> 00:37:52,622
Thank you.

467
00:37:53,424 --> 00:37:55,659
There's just one thing I want clarified.

468
00:37:57,094 --> 00:37:58,528
What is it?

469
00:37:59,197 --> 00:38:01,778
Is something going on between you and Liam?

470
00:38:06,070 --> 00:38:09,282
Are you having an affair with my boyfriend?

471
00:38:10,441 --> 00:38:12,024
What?

472
00:38:18,036 --> 00:38:21,063
Are you having an affair with my boyfriend?

473
00:38:22,314 --> 00:38:23,849
What?

474
00:38:26,290 --> 00:38:27,824
No.

475
00:38:30,861 --> 00:38:34,998
No. Nothing's going on between Liam and me.

476
00:38:36,400 --> 00:38:42,239
When we were at your resort,
Liam got so drunk.

477
00:38:43,236 --> 00:38:45,671
He called me Joyce.

478
00:38:47,378 --> 00:38:51,415
Back then, I didn't know who Joyce was.

479
00:38:52,495 --> 00:38:57,899
Then, I found out that you are Joyce.

480
00:39:01,842 --> 00:39:05,830
Via, I don't know either.

481
00:39:05,830 --> 00:39:13,036
Liam... Liam has known my real name
for a long time now.

482
00:39:14,639 --> 00:39:18,276
College. We met during college.

483
00:39:18,276 --> 00:39:19,744
We were classmates in college.

484
00:39:19,744 --> 00:39:20,945
So you have a past.

485
00:39:20,945 --> 00:39:23,001
We don't have a past.

486
00:39:26,083 --> 00:39:28,252
Via, believe me, please.

487
00:39:28,252 --> 00:39:30,488
I want to.

488
00:39:30,488 --> 00:39:32,490
Oh my God.

489
00:39:34,467 --> 00:39:36,201
Please, Via.

490
00:39:37,528 --> 00:39:39,964
Are you mad?

491
00:39:39,964 --> 00:39:43,200
Are you mad because of what I asked you?

492
00:39:43,200 --> 00:39:45,402
No, I'm not...

493
00:39:47,172 --> 00:39:52,377
It's okay if you're mad, Savana.

494
00:39:53,711 --> 00:39:58,707
So you'll also know
how it feels to be wrongly accused.

495
00:40:23,207 --> 00:40:25,142
I'm sorry.

496
00:40:26,772 --> 00:40:31,809
I thought Joyce already knew
you were no longer in Blacksmith.

497
00:40:36,354 --> 00:40:38,121
I want to go home.

498
00:40:55,630 --> 00:40:57,064
Hey.

499
00:41:00,745 --> 00:41:02,679
Is everything all right?

500
00:41:05,375 --> 00:41:06,609
Hey.

501
00:41:08,847 --> 00:41:10,955
Want to go somewhere else?

502
00:41:10,955 --> 00:41:12,527
I'll go with you.

503
00:41:18,896 --> 00:41:21,831
Sorry, Hans, but I want to go home.

504
00:41:24,101 --> 00:41:25,569
What happened?

505
00:41:25,569 --> 00:41:27,405
Okay.

506
00:41:27,405 --> 00:41:29,839
- I want to go home.
- Okay, okay.

507
00:41:31,108 --> 00:41:33,109
Please.

508
00:41:42,286 --> 00:41:44,120
I'll drive you home.

509
00:41:58,302 --> 00:42:01,037
I'm having a hard time.

510
00:42:02,032 --> 00:42:04,767
This is not the life I chose.

511
00:42:08,178 --> 00:42:10,246
This is not me.

512
00:42:13,463 --> 00:42:15,855
I want to go home!

513
00:42:15,855 --> 00:42:18,857
Then go home. It's so simple.

514
00:42:30,025 --> 00:42:31,559
Bro.

515
00:42:35,005 --> 00:42:40,476
I wish it was that easy, Intoy.

516
00:42:43,714 --> 00:42:47,651
Bro, there's a mountain of trash.

517
00:42:47,651 --> 00:42:49,385
Everything is there...

518
00:42:49,385 --> 00:42:52,848
Carton, plastic, bottle, diaper, poop.

519
00:42:52,848 --> 00:42:55,826
Everything is there
because it's a mountain of trash.

520
00:42:55,826 --> 00:43:01,798
And me? I'm underneath.

521
00:43:06,136 --> 00:43:07,537
Why?

522
00:43:09,006 --> 00:43:10,507
What do you mean "why"?

523
00:43:10,507 --> 00:43:13,309
I was buried under the trash.

524
00:43:16,813 --> 00:43:18,382
Sorry, I didn't know.

525
00:43:18,382 --> 00:43:20,817
You're not listening.

526
00:43:20,817 --> 00:43:23,886
I was buried under a mountain of trash.

527
00:43:25,910 --> 00:43:28,845
Do you know what I told myself?

528
00:43:31,261 --> 00:43:33,868
Ask me what I told myself.

529
00:43:33,868 --> 00:43:35,033
What did you tell yourself?

530
00:43:35,033 --> 00:43:37,445
I told myself...

531
00:43:38,952 --> 00:43:40,857
"I will go home".

532
00:43:42,906 --> 00:43:45,108
I did it, bro.

533
00:43:45,108 --> 00:43:52,081
I forced myself out.
I climbed my way up to the top.

534
00:43:53,850 --> 00:43:59,623
And when I got out, I took a deep breath.

535
00:44:02,092 --> 00:44:04,795
It still smelled like trash.
It still smelled like poop.

536
00:44:04,795 --> 00:44:07,430
I said, "I'm not going to die here".

537
00:44:11,468 --> 00:44:13,724
I'll go home. But...

538
00:44:17,138 --> 00:44:19,075
But to where?

539
00:44:22,579 --> 00:44:28,684
Bro, wherever you think home is.

540
00:45:24,710 --> 00:45:29,748
Sir Liam, do stars grow old?

541
00:45:30,847 --> 00:45:32,448
Yes.

542
00:45:33,483 --> 00:45:37,854
But it grows old very slowly.

543
00:45:37,854 --> 00:45:41,291
They live for a long time?

544
00:45:41,291 --> 00:45:43,794
Very long.

545
00:45:43,794 --> 00:45:46,530
They live millions of years.

546
00:45:46,530 --> 00:45:51,968
Wow, I wish I was a star.

547
00:45:51,968 --> 00:45:53,669
Why?

548
00:45:54,304 --> 00:46:04,904
So that I can spend millions of years
with my parents before they die.

549
00:46:10,854 --> 00:46:12,355
Sep.

550
00:46:12,355 --> 00:46:15,025
I wish we were all stars.

551
00:46:15,025 --> 00:46:22,689
Even though we know we will lose someone,

552
00:46:22,689 --> 00:46:25,202
we can still make the most of our time
with them.

553
00:46:25,202 --> 00:46:30,139
Because we'll spend a long time with them.

554
00:46:32,075 --> 00:46:34,677
That's what I said.

555
00:46:36,279 --> 00:46:39,882
Do you have a problem, Sir Liam?

556
00:46:43,920 --> 00:46:45,588
Yes.

557
00:46:47,424 --> 00:46:51,260
When someone gets old, his problems pile up.

558
00:46:52,295 --> 00:46:57,700
So sometimes, I wish I was a star.

559
00:47:04,641 --> 00:47:11,086
My mom had so many problems, too.

560
00:47:11,086 --> 00:47:15,585
My dad had heart disease,
but we didn't have money for his medicines.

561
00:47:15,585 --> 00:47:17,587
So this is what I did.

562
00:47:17,587 --> 00:47:19,389
He said he felt better.

563
00:47:19,389 --> 00:47:24,727
He said his loved ones make him feel better.

564
00:47:26,129 --> 00:47:30,633
Is the pain in your chest getting better,
Sir Liam?

565
00:47:32,355 --> 00:47:34,089
It does get better.

566
00:47:34,838 --> 00:47:36,572
So much.

567
00:47:38,809 --> 00:47:46,809
I remember someone
who looks exactly like you.

568
00:47:48,185 --> 00:47:51,337
Oh, so there's someone else
as good-looking as me.

569
00:47:54,026 --> 00:47:56,693
Not just as handsome as you.

570
00:47:56,693 --> 00:47:58,794
He's also as kind as you.

571
00:48:09,139 --> 00:48:11,141
This is what we'll do, Edison.
Someone will walk by.

572
00:48:11,141 --> 00:48:12,676
I want a continuous shot.

573
00:48:12,676 --> 00:48:16,346
Here, here, here. Like this.

574
00:48:16,346 --> 00:48:17,848
Are you ready, Josh?

575
00:48:17,848 --> 00:48:18,982
Of course.

576
00:48:18,982 --> 00:48:21,785
I was born ready. You know that.

577
00:48:25,257 --> 00:48:26,803
- Dee? Dee?
- What happened?

578
00:48:26,803 --> 00:48:29,525
- What happened to you?
- Hurry up! Call someone!

579
00:48:30,393 --> 00:48:31,728
Hi, Director Phil!

580
00:48:31,728 --> 00:48:33,563
Hi.

581
00:48:33,563 --> 00:48:35,365
Megan sent me the script.

582
00:48:35,365 --> 00:48:38,869
Congratulations. It's our first big day.
And it's a big scene!

583
00:48:38,869 --> 00:48:43,573
This is an exciting day, right, Savana?

584
00:48:43,573 --> 00:48:45,208
I should call you Joyce.

585
00:48:45,208 --> 00:48:47,504
I have to get used to it.

586
00:48:49,179 --> 00:48:51,181
Hi, Director Phil.

587
00:48:51,181 --> 00:48:52,382
Who can perform first-aid?

588
00:48:52,382 --> 00:48:53,829
Medic!

589
00:48:53,829 --> 00:48:56,152
- Please help her!
- Let me do it.

590
00:48:56,887 --> 00:48:58,188
- Medic!
- Deedee!

591
00:48:58,188 --> 00:49:00,023
- Medic?
- Okay, okay, wait.

592
00:49:00,023 --> 00:49:01,224
I got this.

593
00:49:01,224 --> 00:49:03,529
One, two, three.

594
00:49:03,529 --> 00:49:05,826
One, two, three!

595
00:49:07,831 --> 00:49:09,432
This girl loves eating. That's why.

596
00:49:09,432 --> 00:49:11,735
My gosh, Dee.

597
00:49:11,735 --> 00:49:13,402
Sorry.

598
00:49:14,037 --> 00:49:15,538
Thank you.

599
00:49:15,538 --> 00:49:16,940
But that's impressive.

600
00:49:16,940 --> 00:49:18,041
You're great.

601
00:49:18,041 --> 00:49:19,204
Very good.

602
00:49:22,681 --> 00:49:25,348
By the way, this is Sep.

603
00:49:25,348 --> 00:49:30,287
Liam and I met him at the orphanage.

604
00:49:30,287 --> 00:49:33,623
He asked us to bring him here to the set.

605
00:49:33,623 --> 00:49:37,861
We asked for permission from the nuns.
And luckily, they allowed us.

606
00:49:37,861 --> 00:49:40,463
Promise, Director. I'll behave.

607
00:49:40,463 --> 00:49:43,466
I just want to watch the filming.

608
00:49:43,466 --> 00:49:46,009
Really? When I say "Quiet on the set",

609
00:49:46,009 --> 00:49:47,637
you stay quiet, okay?

610
00:49:47,637 --> 00:49:48,972
Promise, Director Phil.

611
00:49:48,972 --> 00:49:50,506
Promise?

612
00:50:02,819 --> 00:50:04,428
I can't let you do this.

613
00:50:04,428 --> 00:50:07,156
I love him, Dad.

614
00:50:07,156 --> 00:50:08,540
- Via!
- Spoiled brat!

615
00:50:08,540 --> 00:50:10,962
What do you know about love?

616
00:50:10,962 --> 00:50:12,764
Dad, please. No, no, no, please!

617
00:50:12,764 --> 00:50:15,633
No! Don't! Not Liam, please.

618
00:50:15,633 --> 00:50:16,901
I love him!

619
00:50:16,901 --> 00:50:18,812
Stop!

620
00:50:22,240 --> 00:50:23,875
You're being like that...

621
00:50:23,875 --> 00:50:28,446
You think about nothing but power and money,

622
00:50:28,446 --> 00:50:30,682
because you lost Mom, right?

623
00:50:30,682 --> 00:50:32,750
Don't drag your mom into this.

624
00:50:32,750 --> 00:50:36,120
I wish I had gone with Mom.

625
00:50:36,120 --> 00:50:38,456
That only changed because of Liam.

626
00:50:38,456 --> 00:50:42,560
So if you want to take him away from me, go.

627
00:50:42,560 --> 00:50:45,729
Go ahead. Kill me first.

628
00:50:55,373 --> 00:50:58,325
Medic!
